< \paragraph{Interruption and decision.}
< The incomplete share is partly a cost of answering under a cap. When the best option is written and ranked first, the answer picks it in 45--89\% of complete traces but 14--62\% of unfinished ones, and in unfinished traces this rate does not rise with the tokens written since the best option's value (if anything it falls, $p=0.06$). Restricting to five-option menus, where every median finish is within budget, the incomplete share is still 26--63\% for the Qwen models. The models rarely stop before the cap on their own, and when they do they are right in at least 97.6\% of cases, so the unforced run cannot separate the two for them. Granite-8B stops on its own in every trace and keeps the same pattern without forcing: of its unforced gap, 55\% is passed over, 27\% arithmetic, 14\% unreached and 4\% incomplete.
---
> \paragraph{Truncation and decision.}
> Not reached and incomplete together are budget effects: 74--79\% of the gap for the Qwen models, 47\% for DeepSeek-8B and 17\% for Phi-mini and Granite-8B. When the best option is written and ranked first, the answer picks it in 45--89\% of complete traces but 14--62\% of unfinished ones, and in unfinished traces this rate does not rise with the tokens written since the best option's value (if anything it falls, $p=0.06$). Restricting to five-option menus, where every median finish is within budget, the incomplete share is still 26--63\% for the Qwen models. Traces without truncation separate the two. Among unforced traces that finish the list (458--612 per model), the answer passes over the trace's best option in 50\% for Phi-mini and 40\% for Granite-8B, against 6--9\% for the other four; forced traces that finish within 600 tokens give 51\% and 43\% against 7--17\%. So passing over a finished comparison is a real failure for two models and a minor one for the rest, whose loss is mostly the budget. Granite-8B stops on its own in every trace, and its unforced gap splits 55\% passed over, 27\% arithmetic, 14\% unreached and 4\% incomplete.
